 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Mechanism:** context-local proxies. Werkzeug `LocalProxy` objects wrap a single `ContextVar`, and each proxy resolves its target when it's accessed.\n\nIn `src/tessel/globals.py`:\n\n- `_app_var` (line 40) is the `ContextVar[AppContext]` named `\"tessel.app_ctx\"`. It holds the current `AppContext`.\n- `app_ctx` (line 41) is a `LocalProxy` directly onto `_app_var`, so it resolves to the `AppContext` itself.\n- `active_app` (line 44) is `LocalProxy(_app_var, \"app\")`. It resolves to the `Tessel` app via `AppContext.app`.\n- `g` (line 47) is `LocalProxy(_app_var, \"g\")`. It resolves to the `_AppCtxGlobals` instance via `AppContext.g`.\n- `request` (line 57) is `LocalProxy(_app_var, \"request\")`. It resolves to the `Request` via `AppContext.request`.\n- `session` (line 60) works the same way, via `AppContext.session`.\n\nThe `AppContext` is set in `_app_var` when a context is pushed, for example with `app.app_context()` or while a request is handled. Because it's a `ContextVar`, each thread or async task sees its own value.\n\nIf nothing is pushed, the proxy raises `RuntimeError` with `_no_app_msg` (for `active_app` and `g`) or `_no_req_msg` (for `request` and `session`).\n\nThe `request_ctx` name is deprecated and now just returns `app_ctx`, because the request and app contexts have been merged.\n\nI didn't open `ctx.py`, where `AppContext` is defined and pushed, so the push/pop details are unverified.",
